{
  "name": "@commonfabric/patterns",
  // How to test in this package. Pick the route by what the test needs, drop
  // the file in the matching place, and the route's runner discovers it on its
  // own. A focused browser regression is the one explicit exception because
  // its real-DOM entry point must be named for deno-web-test.
  //
  // Lane 1 — plain Deno unit test. A `*.test.ts` file of pure logic (helpers,
  // parsing, schema/string utilities) that runs under `deno test` with no
  // Common Fabric runtime, shell, toolshed, or browser. Put it anywhere in the
  // package except an `integration/` directory. The `deno-test` task below
  // picks up every `**/*.test.ts` outside `integration/` apart from the
  // browser files, so adding a unit test is just adding the file. It resolves
  // imports the way the rest of the workspace does, and it is not sharded.
  // Examples: vehicles.test.ts, cfc/prompt-injection/prompt.test.ts.
  //
  // Focused browser regression — a `*.browser.test.ts` file for DOM behavior
  // that is too narrow for the running-shell integration lane. The name is
  // what routes it: `deno-test` ignores the glob, and `browser-test` hands the
  // same glob to deno-web-test. The root `deno task test` and workspace "Test"
  // CI job compose Lane 1 and this real-browser route for the package.
  //
  // Lane 2 — pattern test (the testing and coverage docs call these "pattern
  // unit tests"). A `*.test.tsx` file that `export default`s a pattern (or
  // `multiUserTest(...)`) which drives a real pattern through `action(...)`
  // steps and `assert_*` `computed(...)` checks. It is run by `cf test`, which
  // instantiates it in the runtime; it is not a `deno test`. Colocate it next
  // to the pattern it exercises. The `.tsx` extension alone routes it here: the
  // `test` task's `**/*.test.ts` glob never matches `.test.tsx`. CI runs these
  // in the "Pattern Unit Tests" job, assigned to chunks by a stable filename
  // hash (the `pattern-tests` target in tasks/integration.ts), and they are the
  // only source of authored-pattern coverage (see docs/development/COVERAGE.md).
  //
  // Lane 3 — integration test. A `*.test.ts` file under `integration/` that
  // needs a running shell/toolshed/browser (PiecesController, ShellIntegration,
  // end-to-end flows). It is run by `deno task integration`. CI runs these in
  // the "Pattern Integration Tests" job across its shard matrix. Measured
  // files have weights in tasks/select-pattern-integration-files.ts.
  // Unmeasured files receive the default weight. Reload-specific cases live
  // in integration/reload/ and run via `integration:reload`.
  //
  // Every workspace member must define a `test` task. The root runner
  // (tasks/test.ts) calls `deno task test` in each member, and a member with no
  // such task would fall through to the root task and recurse over the whole
  // workspace; the runner refuses to start rather than let that happen, and
  // names the member. So this lane stays a real task, never an empty stub.
  //
  // For how to write each kind of test and how CI measures them, see
  // docs/development/TESTING.md (the testing hub),
  // docs/common/workflows/pattern-testing.md (writing pattern tests), and
  // docs/development/COVERAGE.md (how the lanes feed the coverage-debt gate).
  "tasks": {
    "integration": "LOG_LEVEL=warn deno test --shuffle=$(deno task -q test-seed) --v8-flags=--max-old-space-size=4096 --trace-leaks -A $INTEGRATION_TEST_FLAGS ./integration/*.test.ts",
    "integration:reload": "LOG_LEVEL=warn deno test --shuffle=$(deno task -q test-seed) --v8-flags=--max-old-space-size=4096 --trace-leaks -A $INTEGRATION_TEST_FLAGS ./integration/reload/*.test.ts",
    "integration:all": "TEST_HTTP=1 TEST_LLM=1 LOG_LEVEL=warn deno test --shuffle=$(deno task -q test-seed) --v8-flags=--max-old-space-size=4096 --trace-leaks -A ./integration/*.test.ts",
    // The focused browser pass exercises the React event boundary in a real
    // DOM. The `*.browser.test.ts` name is what routes a file there: the same
    // glob keeps it out of the Deno-only pass, so only executed tests count.
    "browser-test": "deno run --allow-env --allow-read --allow-write --allow-run --allow-net ../deno-web-test/cli.ts **/*.browser.test.ts",
    "test": "deno run --allow-read --allow-run=\"$(deno eval \"console.log(Deno.execPath())\")\" ../../tasks/run-member-tests.ts deno-test browser-test",
    "deno-test": "deno test --shuffle=$(deno task -q test-seed) -A --ignore='**/*.test.tsx' --ignore='integration' --ignore='**/*.browser.test.ts' ."
  },
  // File discovery for the `deno-test` task (lane 1). `include` keeps only
  // `.test.ts`, so pattern tests (`.test.tsx`, lane 2) are never collected;
  // `exclude` drops every `integration/` directory (lane 3), which the
  // `integration` task runs instead. These globs apply only to bare `deno test` (the `test` task);
  // the `integration*` tasks pass explicit paths, which Deno does not filter
  // through `exclude`. The `test` task runs with -A because some unit tests
  // spawn a hermetic deno/cf subprocess (for example a compiler check).
  "test": {
    "include": ["**/*.test.ts"],
    "exclude": ["**/integration"]
  },
  "exports": {
    ".": "./mod.ts"
  },
  "imports": {
    // Dependency guide: ../../docs/development/DEPENDENCIES.md
    // Interface-only and side-effect free. The multi-runtime harness worker
    // uses this to hand the runtime→OTel bridge the ambient tracer and meter.
    "@opentelemetry/api": "npm:@opentelemetry/api@^1.9.1",
    "@xyflow/react": "npm:@xyflow/react@^12.11.5",
    // The browser-measurement helper parses authored and compiled Topics
    // sources with it, so no hand-written scanner decides what is code.
    "typescript": "npm:typescript@6.0.3"
  }
}
